# Host session safety (operator workstation)

## The rule

Agents must not damage the operator's interactive Windows/macOS/Linux desktop
session. Lab and Hyper-V work must not cost open browser tabs, startup apps, or
user session state.

## Forbidden without explicit same-message consent

- Writing/deleting `StartupApproved\Run` or `StartupApproved\StartupFolder`
  (HKCU/HKLM) to disable startups
- Mass-disabling Task Manager "Startup apps"
- Stopping/disabling user tray apps (iCUE, Logitech, Snagit, etc.) as a side
  effect of "cleanup"
- `shutdown` / `Restart-Computer` / `Stop-Computer` / forced logoff
- Clearing browser profile data, session restore files, or killing browser
  processes "to free RAM"
- DISM/optional-feature changes that require reboot UNLESS the user explicitly
  asked to install that feature or fix that payload; even then, prefer
  `-NoRestart` and tell the user to reboot when ready — never surprise reboot
- "Optimize" or "cleanup" scripts that touch HKCU Run keys broadly

## Required

- Before any host reboot is recommended, warn that open browser tabs and unsaved
  UI state may be lost; offer to wait
- Hyper-V / lab disk work stays on D:/E:; do not "fix" the user profile to make
  lab work succeed
- If startups are found disabled, restore them; do not leave them disabled
- Origin: 2026-07-16 BEAVIS2 Hyper-V lab session — StartupApproved mass-disable
  + lost browser tabs

## Allowed

- Explicit user request: "reboot now", "disable startup X", "kill chrome"
- Per-test sandboxes / TempDir (not the interactive user session)